1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:03,200
At low tide, you only need one answer:

2
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:04,800
when's the water coming back?

3
00:00:04,910 --> 00:00:06,850
And out here, there's no signal.

4
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:10,050
Tidewatch keeps that answer on your phone.

5
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,200
Your favorite spots sit at the top,

6
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:14,150
each with how far away it is.

7
00:00:15,030 --> 00:00:17,050
You get the next high water
straight away:

8
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:20,100
7:48 AM,
9.4 feet

9
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:23,050
A curve shows the
whole day, with a
marker for now

10
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,300
and every high and
low is listed.

11
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:27,350
Now lose
your signal.

12
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:28,950
Nothing changes.

13
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:31,200
The tide data is
already on your phone,

14
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:32,550
two years of it.

15
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:35,750
Unlock every station
$4.99

16
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:36,950
You pay once.

17
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:38,350
No account
to make,

18
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:40,000
and no ads
to skip.

19
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:42,450
So you can head out, tie off,

20
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,350
and know when the water's coming back.

21
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:47,600
Tidewatch. Know the water.
